00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.510 align:start position:0%
 
war  war never changes over the course of 16  games call of duty has become one of the  world's biggest gaming franchises  although many players may have their own  personal favorites in the series none is  as vastly popular as the modern warfare  sub-series with the modern warfare 2  reboot just around the corner these are  10 things you didn't know about modern  warfare 2019  number 10 teddy bears of war when  playing on the gunfight map trench  random numbers can be found scratched  onto various surfaces around the map and  switch every time the map is reloaded go  to the bunker and shoot the numbers into  the keypad and the door will open  to reveal the most nefarious teddy bears  and other stuffed toys situated around  the war table making plans  exploring the bunker further leads to a  locked door with a code right next to a  telephone in the room input the code  into the keypad and voila the phone next  to the door will ring if you answer the  caller on the other end will immediately  hang up and the secret door will unlock  revealing a giant teddy bear the stuffed  foe is not happy to be disturbed however  firing two miniguns that deal real  damage  and then explodes  number nine pied piper on the cheshire  park map five mouse traps appear  randomly throughout the level after  shooting the last trap it will turn into  a piece of cheese look for the grocer  and find the wheel of cheese with the  chunk missing  okay so i made this sound way too easy  when i was writing this out first of all  each mouse trap spawns individually so  you have to do the first to get the  second they're not all on the same map  at the same time second the wheel of  cheese is in the grocer yes but it might  also be in seven different places around  the map depending on where it spawns  like the fish and chips restaurant which  is where i found it so if you're trying  to do this easter egg all i can say  is good luck  next go to the fountain in the middle of  garden square and press the button to  place offering candles should appear  around the statue and rats should start  pouring out from the left bench all you  have to do now is sit back and enjoy the  show  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  number eight call of duty kaiju if you  thought that godzilla and king kong were  the first massive monsters to show up in  a call of duty game  guess again if you load up the station  map with the overkill perk and lmgs in  both weapon slots head to the concrete  walls on the side of the train station  shoot the six walls until they crumble  each revealing a number and the final a  keypad from left to right shoot the  numbers into the keypad and then turn  around and hop on top of the train to  see what happens  [Music]  [Music]  number seven catch phrases throughout  the course of modern warfare there are  auditory references to the previous  modern warfare titles when practicing  alex's sniping skills during the mission  highway of death after hitting the  watermelon target hadir states that  that's  that  this is a word for word reference to  gaz's line during the tutorial of call  of duty 4 modern warfare your fruit  killing skills are remarkable another  line for line delivery is during the  mission going dark in the game a  disoriented player gets pulled to their  feet by captain price he shouts  we are leaving this quote is only one  word off from his iconic on your feet  soldier we are leaving during the crew  expendable mission in the original  modern warfare he also hearkens back to  another crew expendable line when  entering the electronics store during  the piccadilly circus mission price  relays the order check those corners the  same order he gives during the beginning  of crew expendable check close corners  in a cut scene for going dark when  approaching a police roadblock captain  price describes his plan  this refers to a famous mission in the  original modern warfare in which a nuke  takes out a marine squadron in real life  shock in awe was also the name for the  type of military operation that the  united states used during the iraq war  number six  proto-verdansk before the official  release of warzone you could get a sneak  peek at the entire verdansk map  gamespot's call of duty commissioner  aaron sampson was able to fly out of the  constraints of the multiplayer map  superstore to find a prototype map of  verdansk for call of duty warzone  assuming that this boundary break was  available at launch in october of 2019  fans could get a sneak peek into what  was to come five months before war zone  dropped in march of 2020  number five lawyer up introduced in 2019  during the first season of modern  warfare's multiplayer the introduction  of operator mara caused writer and  photographer clayton hagan to sue  infinity ward according to polygon hagen  filed a copyright infringement lawsuit  in the texas court claiming that mara  was based on a character in one of his  short stories hagen's lawyers stated in  addition to hiring the same talent they  also hired the same makeup professional  who had prepared the talent for hagen's  kade janus photographs they instructed  the makeup professional to prepare the  talent exactly as she had done for  hagin's kate janna's photographs they  instructed her to style the talent's  hair exactly as she had done for hegen's  kate janus photographs even using the  same hairpiece extension initially  published in february of 2021 the  polygon article didn't note any  resolution to the case  i couldn't find any additional  information on how the case was settled  either  number four mini-map attack during the  playstation exclusive beta for modern  warfare infinity ward eradicated the  mini-map from the hud unless a uiview  was deployed in competitive play instead  of the classic mini-map they relied on  sound design and an in-game compass to  let players find each other however the  player response was so strong that  infinity ward quickly re-implemented the  mini-map within a few days although a  controversy at the time of its  implementation most pro players praised  infinity ward for their communication  and quick compromises concerning player  feedback what was left over though in  the final game was a confusing hybrid  system where players could appear on  either the original compass or mini-map  or both depending on a large number of  factors  number three so here i am during the  piccadilly circus mission one of the  dead bodies has a very familiar looking  tattoo the iconic logo belongs to  neversoft the now disbanded development  team behind the tony hawk series of  games  number two honing your skills during the  sequences where you play as the younger  version of pharah she is not as  tactically aware and refined in her  skills as a soldier higher recoil slower  reloads and an inability to reload while  aiming down sights all add to the  immersion of her inexperience another  layer of detail comes during the  flashbacks when she is held as a  prisoner of war her exhaustion  malnourishment and torture add to her  lack of mobility  number one  back to the north pole captain price on  the winter docks multiplayer map if you  shoot the weather vane on top of the  clock tower right at midnight a  lightning bolt will strike the vein this  will cause a surge of electricity to  ripple over the power lines and spawn  santa into the map santa will fly by for  a second and then disappear with two  lines of flames burning behind him just  like in the movie back to the future  that's not the end of the secret though  because something isn't quite right  about jolly old saint nick and his  trusted reindeer rudolph the closer look  at the sleigh unveils that santa is  captain price and rudolph is riley from  call of duty ghosts  although call of duty games get a  reputation for being thrown together  because of their yearly release schedule  the 2019 reboot of modern warfare proves  that infinity ward could put together a  new style of call of duty game with a  well-planned year full of maps modes and  weapon releases the level of detail fun  and goofy secrets throughout the game  elevate the entire experience to  something more than just another call of  duty game in fact the animations and  attention to detail were so well done  that both call of duty cold war and call  of duty vancard kept the same animations  from modern warfare 2019. it's been a  blast uncovering the intricacies and  secrets of development and the  controversies and hidden treasures  surrounding the game itself check out  our everything to know guide if you're  hyped for call of duty modern warfare 2.  catch me on twitter at stewie review and  for all things video games keep it here  at gamespot

